+     *  leftmost bits with 0s (i.e., it is exactly the same as an unsigned
+     *  right shift).  This means that when `a' is negative, `sa' ends up
+     *  with the value 1 rather than -1.  After that, everything else goes
+     *  wrong.
+     */
